  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "As ye have therefore received Christ Jesus the Lord, so walk ye in Him: rooted and built up in Him, and stablished in the faith. Christian discipleship begins with receiving Christ by faith and progresses by living in unbroken dependence upon Him through prayer, Word study, and active service, putting on the whole armor of God against demonic deception.",
      "density": 3.4179,
      "words": 59,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 34,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The totality of deity in a body. First principle: Isaiah's Mighty God and John's Word-made-flesh conclude here — fullness bodily, not metaphorically; the incarnation is theodicy and theology at once.",
      "density": 2.2143,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The hidden mystery is revealed to saints. First principle: Romans 16 and Colossians 1 open the same sealed book — the mystery is Christ's indwelling plan, timed for the apostolic age.",
      "density": 2.1464,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Reconciliation spans earth and heaven. First principle: the cross's peace is cosmic in scale and personal in application — the Prince of Peace purchased the reconciliation His name promised.",
      "density": 2.0964,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-3-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Barbarian and Scythian dissolve in the new man. First principle: Galatians' oneness is extended to the empire's extremes — Christ is the all in all, so ethnicity is not a rank.",
      "density": 2.0893,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 23,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The contrary record is erased and nailed up as cancelled. First principle: the debt-document is killed at the scene of the payment — Isaiah's blotting and David's blessed covering happened at Golgotha.",
      "density": 2.0571,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Baptism joins the burial and the rising through faith in God's operation. First principle: the ordinance reenacts the gospel sequence — buried with, raised with; the power is God's, the faith is ours.",
      "density": 2.025,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Preexistence and coherence — the Son holds the cosmos together. First principle: consistency is personal; every atom's persistence is the Word's ongoing work — the Wisdom of Proverbs 8 named.",
      "density": 1.8929,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-3",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The treasure vault is a Person. First principle: Proverbs' wisdom-cry and Isaiah's Spirit-of-wisdom find their treasury in Christ — knowledge is hidden in Him, not in systems.",
      "density": 1.875,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-18",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Beginning and firstborn, so that in all things He has preeminence. First principle: headship and resurrection-prime join — the church's Head is death's Firstborn, and preeminence is His in everything.",
      "density": 1.8357,
      "words": 30,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Shadows precede substance. First principle: the sanctuary system was a silhouette — Hebrews' shadow-language and the tabernacle pattern find their casting body in Christ.",
      "density": 1.8,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The glory-riches mystery is Gentile-located. First principle: the hope is not Christ coming back alone but Christ dwelling within — Immanuel internalized among the nations.",
      "density": 1.7679,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-3-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The risen life seeks the seated Christ. First principle: ascension is the church's orientation — the right-hand session of Psalm 110 is where the affections live.",
      "density": 1.7357,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "He spoiled principalities and powers, making a show of them openly, triumphing over them in it. First principle: the cross is a public victory parade over demonic powers.",
      "density": 1.6143,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Rescue and relocation — the kingdom of the dear Son. First principle: conversion is a transfer of jurisdictions; darkness's authority ends where the Son's kingdom begins.",
      "density": 1.5643,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-3-4",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The appearing reveals the hidden life — saints appear with Him in glory. First principle: Christ as life makes His appearing ours; the hidden-with-Christ reality becomes visible glory.",
      "density": 1.5571,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-2-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The putting off of the body of sins by Christ's circumcision. First principle: the heart-circumcision of Deuteronomy is performed without hands — the flesh-cutting is flesh-removal.",
      "density": 1.5071,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "He is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn of every creature. First principle: Christ reveals the invisible God and has priority over all creation.",
      "density": 1.3929,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 13,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "col-1-16",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "By Him all things were created — visible and invisible. First principle: the Son is agent of creation, not its first creature.",
      "density": 1.2357,
      "words": 22,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 12,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
